[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says: one issue, one fix queued. Its own table says otherwise.
Every report in it is about a booking on the wrong day, so it was merged by
[subject](/kb/triage/dedupe). Placed by their tenant, the reports have two causes, and the fix
queued for #4471 closes only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Fixing the parser leaves the booking-v3 form hint open. Each problem now has its
own ticket.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

The counts are built from the ticket export at render time. Duplicate rows from overlapping
export pages are counted once. Each report is placed by its tenant, the locale they write dates
in and the booking form they run (`#lib/kb/causes`), not by its intake tag and not by its subject.

## The problems

### `parser`: the shared parser reads month first

Every tenant on file writes the day first. The shared parser reads every date month first, so a
date whose day is 12 or lower comes out with day and month swapped: "Our 7 April reminder went
out on 4 July" (R-41200). This is the fix #4471 has queued. It covers every tenant through the
app and email, and the booking-v2 tenants through the form.

Some of these reports read like a date that moved by one day (`desk-notes.json`). Their tenant
and channel place them here, and they stay counted here, with the rest of the parser reports.

### `hint`: the booking-v3 form tells day-first tenants to type month first

Tenants on booking-v3 show `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their people type what the hint
says, month first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The result looks
like `parser` (a swapped day and month), but the parser is not involved: fixing it changes
nothing here. The fix is the hint, and the field's input order, following the tenant's locale.
The table on #4471 already marked this group "not this ticket — no ticket of its own". It has one
now.

## Intake tags are not the cause

Intake tags each report from the reporter's browser, the moment it comes in. The cause depends
on the tenant, and the two disagree: the table shows what intake tagged each problem's reports.
Do not split or count these problems by tag.

## What changes

- Each problem is tracked in its own ticket (linked in the table), with its own count. The fix
  queued for #4471 belongs to `parser`; `hint` needs a fix of its own in booking-v3.
- New reports about a wrong date: look up the tenant before you merge. A report through the form
  at a booking-v3 tenant is `hint`; the rest is `parser`.
- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) accepted that reports with different
  subjects may end up apart. #4471 shows the other side: reports with the same subjects and
  different causes end up together.

